      <activity id="1f94fbbc-b1c5-5ca3-ba15-59c5cc609e99" activityNameId="c8ae7483-75c0-5007-942f-dddcbd6afa1c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Granite, natural stone council, at mine</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Granite, natural stone council, at mine
This dataset reflects granite mining in North America. Some input or output flows are taken from the ecoinvent dataset "limestone, at mine". The input of ammonium nitrate is modelled by the blasting process. The ammonium nitrate consumption is used for conversion.;
UUID: 346be187-5f5a-331d-acec-d8b35ac3ef2a
This dataset includes the material, energy, water and land use of quarrying 1 kg of granite in Switzerland.
Location: Data from North America modelled with Swiss and European datasets.
Technology: Granite mining by drilling, sawing, splitting or blasting of the stone.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: unknown 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_346be187-5f5a-331d-acec-d8b35ac3ef2a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
